syntax:
To define a virtual function in a class, use the 'virtual' keyword in the base class declaration, e.g.:
virtual return_type function_name(parameters) override; // In derived classes, use 'override' for clarity and safety.
Implementation notes: The compiler automatically generates the vtable and vptr; developers don't directly manipulate them. For example, in a class definition:
class Base {
public:
    virtual void virtualFunc();  // Declares a virtual function
};
class Derived : public Base {
public:
    void virtualFunc() override;  // Overrides the virtual function
};
